# What the trace proxy writes to disk: complete prompts in plaintext. Never commit it.
# A glob rather than named directories: naming them means a new one — someone changing
# TRACE_DIR, say — slips through, and what slips through is everybody's full conversations,
# pushed to a remote. The traces-demo sample got in exactly that way.
trace-proxy/traces*/
# Generated CommonJS marker; see scripts/ensure-trace-proxy-cjs.mjs
trace-proxy/package.json

# Real data. Never committed.
data.backup-*/
log/

# Compiled authkey-sync binary (go build drops it next to main.go).
authkey-sync/authkey-sync

notes.md
